Package: soc-ota-agent
Architecture: arm64 armhf amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ${shlibs:Depends},
         ca-certificates,
         curl,
         jq,
         systemd
Recommends: libubootenv-tool
Suggests: grub-common
Description: OTA-Pulse device update agent (bootloader compatibility mode)
 The OTA-Pulse agent polls the OTA-Pulse backend for firmware deployments,
 installs signed A/B root filesystem updates, reports status and inventory,
 and commits or rolls back an update based on the health of the new slot.
 .
 This package is configured for bootloader compatibility mode: the board's
 own bootloader integration (U-Boot or GRUB) owns the boot-slot flag, boot
 counting and rollback. The agent never switches slots itself in this mode
 and refuses to run (fail closed) when it cannot read the bootloader
 environment.
 .
 The package ships the agent, its systemd unit, the configuration template,
 the inventory and identity scripts, the update state scripts that are
 embedded into OTA artifacts, a provisioning helper, and the boot guard: a
 timer that reboots a device whose freshly installed update is still not
 committed after 20 minutes, so that the bootloader reverts it.
 .
 It does not contain a bootloader, partition layout or board support; those
 come from the image the package is installed into.

Package: socmond
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
         ca-certificates,
         curl,
         jq,
         systemd
Description: OTA-Pulse device monitoring daemon
 socmond collects device telemetry (CPU, memory, disk, network, temperature),
 captures crash dumps and reboot reasons, and uploads them to the OTA-Pulse
 backend. It registers itself with a provisioning token and then
 authenticates with its own per-device API key.
 .
 The package ships the daemon, its watchdog, the core dump handler and the
 command line tools soc-ctl and soc-deregister, together with their systemd
 units. The default configuration contains no credentials.
